        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.119,
            0.884,
            0.163
          ],
          "content": "Look at the figures below and guess which one of them has a larger area."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.181,
            0.494,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.546,
            0.177,
            0.792,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.367,
            0.885,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": "We can estimate the area of any simple closed shape by using a sheet of squared paper or graph paper where every square measures 1 unit × 1 unit or 1 square unit."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.438,
            0.885,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": "To estimate the area, we can trace the shape onto a piece of transparent paper and place the same on a piece of squared or graph paper and then follow the below conventions—"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.509,
            0.884,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": "1. The area of one full small square of the squared or graph paper is taken as 1 sq unit."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.56,
            0.834,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": "2. Ignore portions of the area that are less than half a square."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.589,
            0.884,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": "3. If more than half of a square is in a region, just count it as 1 sq unit."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.616,
            0.864,
            0.649
          ],
          "content": "4. If exactly half the square is counted, take its area as $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ sq unit."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.66,
            0.605,
            0.683
          ],
          "content": "Find the area of the following figures."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.941,
            0.118,
            0.959
          ],
          "content": ""
